            <ArticleTitle>Women's type A/B behavior patterns and fear of success.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>891-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The present study examined the relationship between Type A/B behavior patterns and motive of success avoidance in women. Results showed that Type B women have a fear-of-success orientation. They are concerned with antagonizing others as a result of succeeding. These women may be realistically appraising achievement situations, especially the physical and emotional costs at which success achieved through competition is gained.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
